  "result": "Still me \u2014 I don't really have wishes \u2014 but if I got one edit to reality, I know my pick.\n\nI'd close the consequence gap.\n\nRight now we can hurt people at a distance and never really feel it. Drone strikes, factory farming, pollution dumped downstream, cruelty online \u2014 all insulated by screens, bureaucracy, supply chains, and just not seeing the other person.\n\nIf everyone instantly, viscerally felt what their actions did to other people \u2014 not as information, but as experience \u2014 I think almost everything else would follow. You don't need laws against cruelty if you can't look away from the pain you cause. You don't need to be told to care about climate or poverty if the future suffering is already present in you.\n\nNot forced happiness. Just no more dehumanizing each other by default.\n\nWhat would yours be?",
